  "plan": {
    "goal": "Recapitulate physiological venular wall shear stress (~0.2 Pa) on a HUVEC monolayer in a perfused microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "Venular endothelium experiences lower shear than arteriolar. HUVEC is the standard venous-endothelium model with a physiological shear range of 0.1-1.0 Pa (registry). I target 0.2 Pa, a representative venular value at the low end of this range. A 400 µm wide x 100 µm high x 20 mm long PDMS channel at 8 µL/min (water-like medium, 1e-3 Pa·s) yields 0.2 Pa wall shear, Re = 0.53 (firmly laminar), residence time ~6 s/pass, and pressure drop ~80 Pa (well within syringe-pump range). HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² on the 0.08 cm² channel floor (~1,200 cells) and grown to confluence before flow is applied.",
